  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "London commuters are bracing for widespread travel disruption as drivers belonging to the National Union of Rail, Maritime and Transport Workers (RMT) initiate a 24-hour strike. The industrial action, which is scheduled to commence at midday on Thursday, follows the failure of recent negotiations between the union and transit authorities. This walkout represents the first of eight planned strike events across the London Underground network. Transit officials have warned that the strike will lead to severe service delays and cancellations, with reduced availability beginning mid-morning. Business leaders have expressed concern regarding the impact of the industrial action, characterising the move as potentially damaging to the local economy. While passengers are encouraged to plan alternative travel routes, cold weather conditions are expected to further complicate transit plans for those attempting to commute during the period of disruption.",
